From 43b983b270e10f247b50006c467a695023306714 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:28:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 94/98] Outposts: station services can be shot down

Each outpost and NPC conquerable station gets its service structures in
space (fitting, reprocessing, factory, cloning, repair and laboratory),
as in Dominion and Crucible. They can be shot whenever the station
itself can, and they don't die: at 1% structure the service goes offline
until it is repaired to full armour and structure and its shields come
back to 50%.

While a service is offline:
- cloning: no new clone contracts, jump clones or home station moves
  there, and pilots podded with their clone there wake up in their
  starting station
- factory and laboratory: no new jobs, and running ones pause until it's
  back (the two are separate)
- fitting: no fitting modules while docked
- repair and reprocessing: refused

The station lobby greys the service out (OnProcessStationServiceItemChange)
and the owning corp gets StationStateChange. Service items are spawned for
existing stations when their system boots, and on outpost upgrades. They
change hands with the station. /sov siege lists them and
/sov siege repair repairs them.
